{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the children of Gad answered, etc.</b> They needed to repeat the matter back. Also, Scripture says <b>וַיַּעֲנוּ</b> (\"and they answered\") and does not say ״וַיֹּאמְרוּ״ (\"and they said\"), because Moses had said ״וּנְתַתֶּם לָהֶם״ (\"and you shall give them\"), and they were concerned that at that point the giving would begin. Therefore they answered and said that their crossing over armed is a thing they are obligated to do by decree of the supreme King, and it is an obligatory war for them. And as for His saying <b>אֵת אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר ה׳ לַעֲבָדֶיךָ כֵּן נַעֲשֶׂה</b> — we will arm ourselves quickly before YHWH to wage war against His enemies; but the giving is from now. And as for His saying <b>וְאִתָּנוּ אֲחֻזַּת נַחֲלָתֵנוּ</b> — they did not understand Moses' intention in his words as we have explained it. And therefore he immediately gave it to them, and thereby he revealed his intention that his intent in the statement ״וּנְתַתֶּם לָהֶם״ was in their hand, as I have explained." "<b>Or</b> it is possible that even Moses' own intent was that their title to it would not begin except after the condition; and when he saw the strength of their resolve in the good deed, he agreed and gave it to them immediately and at once." "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of Matot</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:01.155001484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}